# Quick Reference: Security Improvements

## 🔴 CRITICAL ISSUES FOUND

### 1. No Error Handling
```javascript
// ❌ BEFORE - Unhandled errors crash app
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([...]); // If this fails, app crashes
});

// ✅ AFTER - Errors are caught and handled
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  try {
    res.json([...]);
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
  }
});
```

---

### 2. No Input Validation
```javascript
// ❌ BEFORE - No validation
app.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  const id = req.params.id; // Could be anything!
  res.json(users[id]);
});

// ✅ AFTER - Input validated
app.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  try {
    const id = validateId(req.params.id); // Returns valid number or throws
    res.json(users[id]);
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(400).json({ error: err.message });
  }
});
```

---

### 3. Missing Security Headers
```javascript
// ❌ BEFORE
// Response has no security headers - vulnerable to XSS, clickjacking

// ✅ AFTER
const helmet = require('helmet');
app.use(helmet()); // Adds 15+ security headers automatically
```

Headers added:
- `Content-Security-Policy` - Blocks inline scripts
- `X-Frame-Options: DENY` - Prevents clickjacking
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` - Prevents MIME sniffing
- `Strict-Transport-Security` - Enforces HTTPS
- And 11 more...

---

### 4. No Rate Limiting
```javascript
// ❌ BEFORE - Anyone can make unlimited requests
// Attacker can send 1M requests and crash server

// ✅ AFTER
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const limiter = rateLimit({ 
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,  // 15 minutes
  max: 100                     // 100 requests per IP
});
app.use(limiter);
```

Result: Attacker limited to 100 requests per 15 minutes

---

### 5. No Input Sanitization
```javascript
// ❌ BEFORE - Vulnerable to XSS injection
// URL: /users?search=<script>alert('xss')</script>
// Script executes in user's browser!

// ✅ AFTER
const xss = require('xss-clean');
app.use(xss()); // Strips dangerous HTML/JavaScript
```

---

### 6. No Payload Size Limits
```javascript
// ❌ BEFORE - Attacker sends 1GB file
