## 5. XML External Entities (XXE) / Broken Object Level Authorization

### Vulnerability in Original
```javascript
// ❌ VULNERABLE - No object-level access control
app.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  const user = users.find(u => u.id === req.params.id);
  res.json(user); // Any user can access any other user's data
});
```

### Fixed in Improved Version
```javascript
// ✅ SECURE - Add object-level authorization
app.get('/users/:id', authMiddleware, (req, res) => {
  const userId = parseInt(req.params.id);

  // Validate ID format
  if (!Number.isInteger(userId) || userId < 1) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid ID' });
  }

  const user = users.find(u => u.id === userId);

  // Check object-level access
  if (user && req.user.id !== userId && req.user.role !== 'admin') {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
  }

  if (!user) {
    return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });
  }

  res.json(user);
});
```

