## Vulnerability 6: Unvalidated Redirects

### ❌ BEFORE (Vulnerable)
```javascript
app.get('/redirect', (req, res) => {
  const url = req.query.url;
  // Attacker can redirect to: ?url=https://malicious.com/phishing
  res.redirect(url);
});
```

**Phishing Attack:**
```
http://myapp.com/redirect?url=https://fake-bank.com
↓
User trusts myapp.com domain
↓
User enters credentials on fake-bank.com
```

### ✅ AFTER (Secure)
```javascript
const url = require('url');

app.get('/redirect', [
  query('url')
    .custom((value) => {
      const whitelist = ['https://example.com', 'https://app.example.com'];
      if (!whitelist.includes(value)) {
        throw new Error('Redirect URL not in whitelist');
      }
      // Validate it's a valid URL
      try {
        new URL(value);
        return true;
      } catch {
        throw new Error('Invalid URL format');
      }
    })
], handleValidationErrors, (req, res) => {
  const redirectUrl = req.query.url;
  res.redirect(redirectUrl);
});
```

