## Vulnerability 7: Missing Security Headers

### ❌ BEFORE (Vulnerable)
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

app.get('/page', (req, res) => {
  res.send('<html><body>Hello</body></html>');
});
```

**Potential Attacks:**
- Clickjacking: Website embedded in `<iframe>`
- MIME-type sniffing: Browser executes as script
- XSS: No Content Security Policy
- Credentials sent over HTTP: No HSTS header

### ✅ AFTER (Secure)
```javascript
const helmet = require('helmet');
const app = express();

// Automatically sets 15+ security headers
app.use(helmet({
  contentSecurityPolicy: {
    directives: {
      defaultSrc: ["'self'"],
      scriptSrc: ["'self'", "'unsafe-inline'"],
      styleSrc: ["'self'", "'unsafe-inline'"],
      imgSrc: ["'self'", 'data:', 'https:'],
    },
  },
  hsts: {
    maxAge: 31536000, // 1 year
    includeSubDomains: true,
    preload: true
  }
}));

app.get('/page', (req, res) => {
  res.send('<html><body>Hello</body></html>');
});
```

**Headers Added:**
```
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff              # Prevent MIME sniffing
X-Frame-Options: DENY                        # Prevent clickjacking
Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self' # Prevent XSS
Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=...      # HTTPS only
X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block              # Enable XSS filter
```

