## Security Checklist for Production Deployment

- [ ] **Environment Variables**: Use `.env` file for sensitive config
  ```bash
  PORT=3000
  NODE_ENV=production
  ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com,https://app.example.com
  JWT_SECRET=<strong-random-secret>
  DATABASE_URL=<secure-connection-string>
  ```

- [ ] **HTTPS Only**: Always use HTTPS in production
  - Enable HSTS header (done by helmet)
  - Use valid SSL/TLS certificates
  - Redirect HTTP to HTTPS

- [ ] **Authentication**: Implement robust auth
  - Use JWT with secure signing (HS256 or RS256)
  - Set short expiration times
  - Implement refresh token rotation
  - Secure token storage (HTTP-only cookies)

- [ ] **Authorization**: Implement role-based access control (RBAC)
  - Verify user permissions on each endpoint
  - Use principle of least privilege
  - Implement endpoint-specific access checks

- [ ] **Database Security**:
  - Use parameterized queries/prepared statements
  - Implement connection pooling
  - Encrypt sensitive data at rest
  - Use strong database credentials
  - Enable database audit logging

- [ ] **API Security**:
  - Version your API (`/api/v1/users`)
  - Use HTTP methods correctly (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
  - Implement pagination (prevent large result sets)
  - Add API key or OAuth2 for service-to-service calls

- [ ] **Data Protection**:
  - Encrypt sensitive data in transit (TLS)
  - Encrypt sensitive data at rest
  - Implement PII (Personally Identifiable Information) masking
  - Follow GDPR/privacy regulations

- [ ] **Monitoring & Logging**:
  - Use centralized logging (ELK, Splunk, CloudWatch)
  - Monitor error rates and anomalies
  - Set up alerts for security events
  - Rotate logs regularly

- [ ] **Dependency Management**:
  ```bash
  npm audit            # Check for vulnerable dependencies
  npm update           # Keep packages updated
  snyk test            # Third-party security scanning
  ```

- [ ] **Testing**:
  - Write unit tests for validation functions
  - Write integration tests for routes
  - Perform security testing (OWASP Top 10)
  - Use tools like `npm-audit`, `snyk`, or `OWASP ZAP`

- [ ] **Configuration**:
  - Never commit secrets to version control
  - Use `.env` files (add to `.gitignore`)
  - Disable debug mode in production
  - Set NODE_ENV=production

