# Quick Reference: Security Best Practices

## 🔒 Authentication

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: Plaintext password
const user = { username: 'john', password: 'password123' };
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Hash password with bcrypt
const bcrypt = require('bcrypt');
const hashedPassword = await bcrypt.hash(password, 10);

// Verify password
const isValid = await bcrypt.compare(inputPassword, hashedPassword);
```

---

## 🛡️ Input Validation

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: No validation
app.post('/users', (req, res) => {
  const user = req.body; // Direct use
  db.insert(user);
});
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Validate everything
app.post('/users', (req, res) => {
  const email = validateEmail(req.body.email);
  const name = validateString(req.body.name, 50);
  db.insert({ email, name });
});
```

---

## 🔐 Error Handling

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: Expose stack traces
app.get('/data', (req, res) => {
  try {
    // code
  } catch (error) {
    res.json({ error: error.stack }); // Stack trace visible!
  }
});
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Generic error to user, detailed logging internally
app.get('/data', (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    // code
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Detailed error:', error.stack); // Log internally
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
  }
});
```

---

## 💾 Database Security

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: SQL Injection vulnerability
const query = `SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '${email}'`;
db.query(query);
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Parameterized query
const query = 'SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?';
db.query(query, [email]);
```

---

## 🌐 CORS

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: Allow all origins
app.use(cors());
// or
app.use(cors({ origin: '*' }));
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Whitelist specific origins
app.use(cors({
  origin: ['https://example.com', 'https://app.example.com'],
  credentials: true,
  methods: ['GET', 'POST']
}));
```

---

## 🔒 Secrets Management

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: Hardcoded secrets
const API_KEY = 'sk_live_abc123xyz789';
const DB_PASSWORD = 'mypassword123';
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Environment variables
const API_KEY = process.env.API_KEY;
const DB_PASSWORD = process.env.DB_PASSWORD;

// In .env (never commit!)
// API_KEY=sk_live_abc123xyz789
// DB_PASSWORD=mypassword123
```

---

## 📝 Logging

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: Logging sensitive data
console.log('User authenticated:', { 
  email, 
  password: user.password, // DON'T!
  creditCard: user.creditCard // DON'T!
});
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Log relevant info without sensitive data
console.log('User authenticated', {
  userId: user.id,
  email: user.email,
  timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
});
```

---

## 🚫 Rate Limiting

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: No rate limiting
app.get('/login', (req, res) => {
  // Anyone can brute force
});
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Rate limit sensitive endpoints
const loginLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 5, // 5 attempts
  message: 'Too many login attempts'
});

app.post('/login', loginLimiter, (req, res) => {
  // Protected
});
```

---

## 🔍 Data Sanitization

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: Direct use of query parameters
const userQuery = req.query.search;
db.find({ name: userQuery }); // NoSQL injection!
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Sanitize and validate
const mongoSanitize = require('express-mongo-sanitize');
app.use(mongoSanitize()); // Remove '$' and '.'

const userQuery = validateString(req.query.search);
db.find({ name: userQuery });
```

---

## 🔗 HTTPS & TLS

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: HTTP only
app.listen(3000);
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: HTTPS with HSTS
const https = require('https');
const fs = require('fs');

const options = {
  key: fs.readFileSync('private-key.pem'),
  cert: fs.readFileSync('certificate.pem')
};

https.createServer(options, app).listen(3000);

// Add HSTS header
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  res.setHeader('Strict-Transport-Security', 'max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains');
  next();
});
```

---

## 📦 Dependency Security

### ❌ DON'T
```json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "*",
    "lodash": "^1.0.0"
  }
}
```

### ✅ DO
```json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "4.18.2",
    "lodash": "4.17.21"
  },
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=18.0.0"
  }
}
```

---

## 🧪 Testing Security

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: No validation tests
test('user creation', () => {
  const res = request(app).post('/users');
  expect(res.status).toBe(201);
});
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Comprehensive security tests
test('should reject invalid email', () => {
  const res = request(app).post('/users')
    .send({ name: 'John', email: 'not-an-email' });
  expect(res.status).toBe(400);
});

test('should require authentication', () => {
  const res = request(app).get('/users');
  expect(res.status).toBe(401);
});

test('should reject large payloads', () => {
  const res = request(app).post('/users')
    .send({ data: 'x'.repeat(50000) });
  expect(res.status).toBe(413);
});
```

---

## 🚨 Security Headers

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: No security headers
app.use(express.json());
app.get('/', (req, res) => res.json({}));
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: All essential security headers
const helmet = require('helmet');
app.use(helmet());

// Results in:
// Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'
// X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
// X-Frame-Options: DENY
// X-XSS-Protection: 0
// Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000; includeSubDomains
// Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
// And more...
```

---

## 📏 Request Size Limits

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: Unlimited body size
app.use(express.json());
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Limited body size
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));
app.use(express.urlencoded({ limit: '10kb' }));
```

---

## 🔄 Process Error Handling

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: Unhandled errors crash server
const server = app.listen(3000);
// Uncaught error → server dies
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Catch all error types
const server = app.listen(3000);

process.on('uncaughtException', (error) => {
  console.error('Uncaught Exception:', error);
  process.exit(1);
});

process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason, promise) => {
  console.error('Unhandled Rejection:', reason);
  process.exit(1);
});

process.on('SIGTERM', () => {
  console.log('Shutting down gracefully...');
  server.close(() => process.exit(0));
});
```

---

## 🔐 Access Control

### ❌ DON'T
```javascript
// Bad: No authorization
app.get('/admin/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json(getAllUsers());
});
```

### ✅ DO
```javascript
// Good: Role-based access control
const adminOnly = (req, res, next) => {
  if (req.user.role !== 'admin') {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
  }
  next();
};

app.get('/admin/users', authenticate, adminOnly, (req, res) => {
  res.json(getAllUsers());
});
```

---

## 🛑 Validation Types Checklist

### String Validation
```javascript
✅ Length (min/max)
✅ Pattern/format (regex)
✅ Allowed values (whitelist)
✅ Encoding (UTF-8)
✅ Trimming whitespace
```

### Number Validation
```javascript
✅ Range (min/max)
✅ Type (integer/float)
✅ Zero/negative handling
✅ Scientific notation
```

### Email Validation
```javascript
✅ Format check (RFC 5322)
✅ Length limits
✅ Domain verification (optional)
✅ Normalization
```

### File Validation
```javascript
✅ File type/MIME
✅ File size
✅ Filename sanitization
✅ Storage location
✅ Scan for malware
```

---

## 📋 Pre-Production Checklist

```
Inputs & Output
□ All inputs validated
□ All outputs encoded
□ Error messages generic

Authentication & Authorization
□ Strong password policy
□ Secure session management
□ Role-based access control
□ Multi-factor authentication (MFA)

Data Protection
□ Encryption in transit (HTTPS)
□ Encryption at rest
□ PII handling
□ Data retention policy

Infrastructure
□ HTTPS enabled
□ Security headers set
□ Rate limiting configured
□ Firewall rules set
□ DDoS protection

Monitoring
□ Error tracking enabled
□ Logs centralized
□ Alerts configured
□ Metrics monitored

Dependencies
□ No vulnerabilities
□ Versions locked
□ Audit automated
□ Updates scheduled
```

---

## 🆘 Common Vulnerabilities & Fixes

| Vulnerability | Quick Fix |
|---|---|
| SQL Injection | Use parameterized queries |
| XSS | Encode output, set CSP |
| CSRF | Use CSRF tokens |
| Brute Force | Rate limiting |
| Info Disclosure | Generic errors + logging |
| DoS | Rate limits + size limits |
| Insecure Auth | Use JWT/OAuth2 properly |
| Weak Crypto | Use bcrypt, not MD5/SHA |
| Hardcoded Secrets | Environment variables |
| Unvalidated Input | Validate everything |

---

## 📚 Learning Resources

- OWASP: https://owasp.org/
- Node.js Security: https://nodejs.org/en/docs/guides/security/
- Express Security: https://expressjs.com/en/advanced/best-practice-security.html
- PortSwigger Web Security: https://portswigger.net/web-security

---

**Remember**: Security is not a feature, it's a requirement! 🔒

