# Before & After Comparison

## Scenario: Handling Common Attacks

### Attack 1: SQL Injection
```
Request: GET /users?filter='; DROP TABLE users; --
```

**BEFORE:**
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  const { filter } = req.query;
  // Query: SELECT * FROM users WHERE name LIKE '%'; DROP TABLE users; --%'
  // ❌ DATABASE DESTROYED!
  res.json(users);
});
```
**Result:** 🔴 CRITICAL - Database destroyed

**AFTER:**
```javascript
app.get('/users',
  query('filter').optional().trim().isLength({ min: 1, max: 50 }),
  handleValidationErrors,
  (req, res) => {
    // Validation fails:
    // Error: "Filter must be between 1 and 50 characters"
    // Returns 400 Bad Request
    // ✅ INJECTION PREVENTED!
  }
);
```
**Result:** 🟢 SAFE - Attack rejected

---

### Attack 2: Large Payload (DoS)
```
Request: POST /users with 100MB JSON body
```

**BEFORE:**
```javascript
app.use(express.json()); // ❌ NO SIZE LIMIT
app.post('/users', (req, res) => {
  // Trying to parse 100MB JSON...
  // Server memory fills up
  // Other requests hang
  // ❌ SERVER CRASHES
});
```
**Result:** 🔴 CRITICAL - Server DoS

**AFTER:**
```javascript
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' })); // ✅ SIZE LIMIT
app.post('/users', (req, res) => {
  // Payload exceeds 10kb
  // Request rejected immediately
  // Returns 413 Payload Too Large
  // ✅ ATTACK MITIGATED
});
```
**Result:** 🟢 SAFE - Attack blocked

---

### Attack 3: XSS (Cross-Site Scripting)
```
Request: POST /users
Body: { "name": "<script>alert('xss')</script>", "email": "test@example.com" }
```

**BEFORE:**
```javascript
app.post('/users', (req, res) => {
  const { name } = req.body; // ❌ NO SANITIZATION
  // name = "<script>alert('xss')</script>"
  // Stored in database as-is
  // When rendered in HTML: executes malicious script
  // ❌ XSS VULNERABILITY
  res.json({ success: true, data: { name } });
});
```
**Result:** 🔴 CRITICAL - XSS vulnerability

**AFTER:**
```javascript
app.post('/users',
  body('name')
    .trim()
    .matches(/^[a-zA-Z\s'-]+$/) // ✅ PATTERN VALIDATION
    .withMessage('Invalid characters'),
  (req, res) => {
    // "<script>..." doesn't match pattern
    // Validation fails
    // Returns 400 Bad Request
    // ✅ XSS PREVENTED
  }
);
```
**Result:** 🟢 SAFE - Attack blocked

---

### Attack 4: Brute Force (Rate Limiting)
```
Request: 1000 login attempts in 10 seconds
```

**BEFORE:**
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // ❌ NO RATE LIMITING
  // All 1000 requests processed
  // Database overloaded
  // Server slows down for legitimate users
  // ❌ BRUTE FORCE ATTACK SUCCEEDS
});
```
**Result:** 🔴 HIGH - Brute force possible

**AFTER:**
```javascript
const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  max: 100 // ✅ MAX 100 REQUESTS PER 15 MIN
});
app.use(limiter);

app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // After 100 requests in 15 minutes
  // Returns 429 Too Many Requests
  // Client IP is rate-limited
  // ✅ BRUTE FORCE PREVENTED
});
```
**Result:** 🟢 SAFE - Attack throttled

---

### Attack 5: Information Disclosure
```
Request: GET /users (expecting to see all user data)
```

**BEFORE:**
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' }
  ]);
  // ❌ EMAIL ADDRESSES EXPOSED TO ALL USERS
  // ❌ PRIVACY VIOLATION
  // ❌ DATA COULD BE HARVESTED
});
```
**Result:** 🔴 MEDIUM - Data leakage

**AFTER:**
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // Return only necessary fields
  const sanitizedUsers = users.map(({ id, name }) => ({ id, name }));
  res.json({
    success: true,
    data: sanitizedUsers,
    count: sanitizedUsers.length
  });
  // ✅ ONLY NECESSARY DATA EXPOSED
  // ✅ PRIVACY PROTECTED
});
```
**Result:** 🟢 SAFE - Only needed data shown

---

### Attack 6: Error Message Information Leakage
```
Request: GET /users?filter=<any invalid input>
```

**BEFORE:**
```javascript
try {
  // ... code that errors
} catch (error) {
  // ❌ FULL ERROR EXPOSED
  res.json({
    error: error.message,
    stack: error.stack // ❌ REVEALS INTERNAL STRUCTURE
  });
}
```
**Response Example:**
```json
{
  "error": "Cannot read property 'name' of undefined",
  "stack": "at /app/routes/users.js:42:15\nat processRequest (/app/middleware/process.js:8:3)"
}
```
**Result:** 🔴 MEDIUM - Information disclosure

**AFTER:**
