# Common Vulnerabilities & How the Improved Code Protects Against Them

## 1. SQL/NoSQL Injection

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  const query = req.query.search;
  // Directly using user input in database query
  db.find({ $where: query });  // VULNERABLE!
});

// Attacker payload:
// /users?search={"$gt":""}  → Returns all users
// /users?search="; DROP TABLE users; //  → Drops table
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
app.get('/users', 
  query('search')
    .optional()
    .trim()
    .isLength({ max: 100 })
    .matches(/^[a-zA-Z0-9\s@\.\-_]*$/)  // Only allow safe chars
    .withMessage('Search term contains invalid characters'),
  handleValidationErrors,
  (req, res) => {
    // Input already validated and sanitized
    const search = req.query.search;
    // Safe to use in queries
  }
);

// Plus mongoSanitize middleware removes $ and . characters
app.use(mongoSanitize());
```

---

## 2. Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  const search = req.query.search;  // No sanitization
  res.json({
    message: `Search results for: ${search}`
  });
});

// If search = "<img src=x onerror='alert(1)'>"
// Response: { message: "Search results for: <img src=x onerror='alert(1)'>" }
// Browser executes JavaScript!
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
app.get('/users',
  query('search')
    .optional()
    .trim()
    .matches(/^[a-zA-Z0-9\s@\.\-_]*$/)  // Reject HTML/JS
    .withMessage('Invalid characters'),
  handleValidationErrors,
  (req, res) => {
    const search = req.query.search;
    // "<img src=x...>" is rejected at validation stage
    // Response: { success: false, errors: [...] }
  }
);

// Plus helmet() adds CSP headers
app.use(helmet());
// Result: Content-Security-Policy prevents inline scripts
```

---

## 3. Denial of Service (DoS) via Large Payloads

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
app.use(express.json());  // No size limit!

// Attacker sends 1GB JSON payload
// Server runs out of memory → CRASH
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));

// Attacker sends 1GB payload
// Response: 413 Payload Too Large (before memory consumed)
```

---

## 4. Brute Force Attacks

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // No rate limiting - attacker can make unlimited requests
  // 1000 requests/second = no problem
  res.json([...]);
});

// Attacker script:
for (let i = 0; i < 1000000; i++) {
  fetch('/users');  // Hampers legitimate users
}
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
const globalLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  max: 100  // Max 100 requests per 15 minutes per IP
});

app.use(globalLimiter);
app.get('/users', strictLimiter, ...);  // Stricter: 10/15min

// Attacker after 100+ requests:
// Response: 429 Too Many Requests
// IP blocked for 15 minutes
```

---

## 5. Information Disclosure via Error Messages

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  try {
    // ...
  } catch (error) {
    // Stack trace exposed to attacker
    res.json({ error: error.stack });
  }
});

// Production response reveals:
// - File paths (/home/user/app/routes/users.js:45)
// - Internal logic flow
// - Library versions
// - Database structure
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  const isDevelopment = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development';

  res.status(err.status || 500).json({
    success: false,
    message: err.message || 'Internal server error',
    // Stack trace only shown in development
    ...(isDevelopment && { stack: err.stack }),
  });
});

// Production response:
// { success: false, message: "Internal server error" }
// No sensitive details exposed!
```

---

## 6. Clickjacking

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
// No X-Frame-Options header
// Attacker can embed app in iframe:
// <iframe src="http://yourapp.com/delete-account"></iframe>
// User clicks through without realizing
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
app.use(helmet());
// Sets: X-Frame-Options: DENY
// Result: Browser prevents framing
// Iframe load fails with error
```

---

## 7. MIME Type Sniffing

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
res.json({ data: userControlledContent });
// Browser might interpret as HTML/JavaScript
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
app.use(helmet());
// Sets: X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
// Result: Browser respects Content-Type header
// JSON stays JSON, can't be interpreted as HTML
```

---

## 8. NoSQL Query Injection (MongoDB)

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
app.get('/search', (req, res) => {
  const name = req.query.name;
  // Directly using user input in MongoDB query
  db.collection('users').find({ name: name });
});

// Attacker payload:
// /search?name[regex]=^admin
// Matches any string starting with 'admin'

// Attacker payload:
// /search?name[$ne]=false
// Returns all documents where name != false (i.e., all)
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
app.use(mongoSanitize());
// This removes $ and . from query strings automatically!

app.get('/search',
  query('name')
    .optional()
    .isString()
    .trim()
    .isLength({ max: 100 })
    .matches(/^[a-zA-Z0-9\s]*$/),  // Only alphanumeric
  handleValidationErrors,
  (req, res) => {
    // Input is now safe: no $ or . characters
    // No regex operators
    // Exact string match only
  }
);
```

---

## 9. Parameter Pollution

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  const limit = req.query.limit;  // Could be array or string
  // limit could be: string, number, array, object...
});

// Attacker: /users?limit=10&limit=10000
// Behavior depends on how developer coded it
// Different from WAF inspection
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
app.get('/users',
  query('limit')
    .optional()
    .isInt({ min: 1, max: 100 })  // Must be integer
    .withMessage('Invalid limit'),
  handleValidationErrors,
  (req, res) => {
    const limit = req.query.limit;  // Always integer
    // /users?limit=10&limit=10000 → validation error
    // Only first value used, and it's validated
  }
);
```

