## 10. Unhandled Exceptions

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // No try-catch
  const users = JSON.parse(req.body);  // Could throw
  res.json(users);
});

// Invalid JSON → Exception thrown
// Server crashes → All users disconnected
// DDOS vulnerability!
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  try {
    const users = JSON.parse(req.body);
    res.json({ success: true, data: users });
  } catch (error) {
    logger.error('Parse error:', error);
    res.status(400).json({
      success: false,
      message: 'Invalid JSON'
    });
  }
});

// Invalid JSON → Caught and logged
// Graceful error response
// Server stays online
```

---

## 11. Timing Attacks

### ❌ Vulnerable Code (Original)
```javascript
app.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  const user = db.findUser(req.params.id);

  if (user.password === req.query.password) {
    // String comparison takes time proportional to match
    // Attacker measures response time to guess password
  }
});

// Attacker can brute force:
// ?password=a   → 1ms (mismatch at 1st char)
// ?password=ad  → 2ms (mismatch at 2nd char)
// ?password=ad7 → 3ms (matches all)
// Reveals password character by character!
```

### ✅ Protected Code (Improved)
```javascript
// 1. Input validation prevents password guessing
query('password')
  .notEmpty()
  .withMessage('Password required'),

// 2. Rate limiting prevents rapid attempts
const strictLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  max: 10  // Only 10 attempts per 15 min
});

// 3. If authentication needed, use secure comparison:
const crypto = require('crypto');
const timingSafeEqual = crypto.timingSafeEqual;

try {
  timingSafeEqual(
    Buffer.from(userPassword),
    Buffer.from(providedPassword)
  );
} catch (e) {
  // Comparison always takes same time
}
```

