## Testing Checklist

```bash
# 1. Test security headers
curl -I http://localhost:3000/api/users
# Look for: Strict-Transport-Security, X-Frame-Options, etc.

# 2. Test rate limiting
for i in {1..101}; do curl http://localhost:3000/api/users; done
# 101st request should get 429 Too Many Requests

# 3. Test input validation
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/users \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"not-an-email"}'
# Should get 400 Bad Request

# 4. Test error handling
curl http://localhost:3000/nonexistent
# Should get 404, not crash

# 5. Test CORS
curl -H "Origin: http://evil.com" -H "Access-Control-Request-Method: GET" \
  -X OPTIONS http://localhost:3000/api/users
# Should be blocked if origin not whitelisted

# 6. Check for vulnerabilities
npm audit
npm audit fix

# 7. Security header grading
# Visit: https://securityheaders.com
# Enter: http://localhost:3000
```

