## Red Flags (Don't Do!)

```javascript
❌ db.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${id}`); // SQL injection
❌ eval(userInput); // Remote code execution
❌ res.send(userData); // Data leakage
❌ console.log(password); // Logging secrets
❌ throw new Error(error.stack); // Stack trace leak
❌ app.get('/users'); // No rate limit = DoS
❌ app.use(cors()); // All origins = CSRF
❌ app.listen(3000, '0.0.0.0'); // Exposed to internet
❌ require('secret-key'); // In source code = exposed
❌ setTimeout(() => {}, 0); // Blocking event loop
```

---

## Green Lights (Do This!)

```javascript
✅ body('email').isEmail().normalizeEmail(); // Validate
✅ try { } catch (e) { handleError(e); } // Error handling
✅ app.use(helmet()); // Security headers
✅ app.use(rateLimit(...)); // Rate limiting
✅ res.json({ data: users }); // Proper JSON
✅ if (!errors.isEmpty()) return res.status(400); // Validate first
✅ process.env.SECRET; // From environment
✅ bcrypt.hash(password); // Hash passwords
✅ jwt.sign(payload, secret); // Sign tokens
✅ app.listen(PORT, 'localhost'); // Restrict binding
```

